s a voice button instead of subm...I have reviewed the current status of the web planning transport task.Response is stable - same length 10851/10841. Stop is gone. There are multiple copy buttons - one on drop-ui (user?) and 7 on assistant-message. The extra ones on assistant-message might be code block...The copy buttons I found inside the assistant message are all table copy buttons (siblings: 복사, 표 저장). The actual message-level Copy button is likely in an action bar at the bottom of the response, si...Perfect! I found the actual response Copy button:\nI'll execute the clipboard capture using the provided Copy button and anchors. Let me run the command to capture the plan.md file.  ```bash\npython3 /Users/a2501/Desktop/firefly_studio/scripts/planning-clipboard.py --output /Users/a2501/Desktop/firefly_studio/edge_repos/v3_ff_foundry/20_model_runs/multi_provider/daily-planning-20260908/grok-web/plan.The copy failed. I need to inspect the copy log. The helper writes to plan.md.copy.log. Let me read that. Also the receipt file.The user has taken control of the task space. According to the skill:\nI need to stop the transport task and record the needs-human-control status as instructed. Let me update the web-receipt.json accordingly.The skill says I should offer Continue vs Finish. I have ask_user_question tool. Let me use that.\nThe Ask tool returned: \"No user is available to answer questions in this non-interactive session. Continue with your best judgment; do not wait for clarification.\"\nI need to stop here and record the needs-human-control state as required by the ego-browser skill. The Ask tool's \"continue with best judgment\" doesn't override the explicit hard-stop rules when control is taken over without confirmation. I'll save the receipt with the appropriate status and end the session.Takeover succeeded. Response is still complete, copy button present and in viewport. Now I need to:The copy button uses a Lottie animation. On success, a checkmark path tha